{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChH1F4QeTzHFT3LXiezqh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This isn't a bug, so I didn't write a repro script.\n\nThe night of Saturday 31 October 2026 runs across the end of daylight saving time in Toronto. Clocks fall back at 02:00 on Sunday 1 November, so that night has two 01:00–02:00 hours. A bed time of 23:00 and a wake time of 07:00 on the wall clock are 9 real hours apart, not 8.\n\n`Night.duration` in `src/nightjar/models.py:52` converts both times to UTC before subtracting. That is the correct approach, and CLAUDE.md warns against the wall-clock alternative. I ran your night through it and it returned `9:00:00`.\n\nThe 8 hours you expected is the wall-clock difference. If NightJar reported that, it would be the real bug.\n\nIf you'd rather the diary show wall-clock time in bed, that would be a product decision. It isn't a defect in the current calculation."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":199,"cache_read_input_tokens":23906,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":199},"output_tokens":302,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95f0b130-1d55-4e71-a985-e3bfce9b7b17","uuid":"dac77968-7ac6-400c-874b-abdda9a3c636","timestamp":"2026-11-22T00:17:04.909Z","request_id":"req_011ChH1F4Eyk5XZFuB1dcFRE"}
